            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 1 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) City Light's residential Time of Use page: a NERC holiday that falls on a Sunday \"is observed on the following Monday\"; one on a Saturday \"remains on that Saturday\". New Year's Day, Independence Day and Christmas Day in scl:rts-2028-01-01-holidays carry no urpx:observanceRule, so each resolves on its actual date and a Saturday one stays on Saturday. The Monday after a Sunday New Year's Day, Independence Day or Christmas Day is carried as a dated urpx:Holiday with urpx:holidayDate: 2032-07-05, 2033-12-26, 2034-01-02, 2038-07-05, 2039-12-26, 2040-01-02. After 2040 each such Sunday holiday needs a further dated entry, until urpx:mondayIfSundayObservance (proposed in urpx-org/urpx#77) can state the rule; the dated entries then come out.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-05T00:00:00"
        }
      }
